{
    "background_story": "Abram was a young nomad who roamed the vast steppes of Mongolia with his tribe. His life was marked by the constant movement of their yurts and the endless skies. Abram's tribe revered him as a skilled horseman and a master of the ancient art of Gidar, a traditional Mongolian wrestling style that emphasized strength, agility, and strategy. Abram's prowess in Gidar earned him the respect of his peers and the admiration of the elders. During the annual Naadam Festival, Abram's tribe would gather to compete in Gidar matches, and he would always emerge victorious, his movements swift and calculated. His reputation as a Gidar champion spread far and wide, and Abram became a symbol of his tribe's strength and resilience.",
